/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
56. 560.8899999999999864 Td
(ï Discrete elements are nothing but the digits such as 10 decimal digits or 26 letters of alphabets and so on.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
56. 547.3899999999999864 Td
(ï Digital systems use physical quantities called signals to represent discrete elements.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
56. 533.8899999999999864 Td
(ï In digital systems, the signals have two discrete values and are therefore said to be binary.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
56. 520.3899999999999864 Td
(ï A signal in digital system represents one binary digit called a bit. The bit has a value either 0 or 1.) Tj
