(NUMBER SYSTEM) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
52. 743.8899999999999864 Td
(Number system is a basis for counting various items. Modern computers communicate and operate with binary numbers which use only the digits 0 & 1. Basic number system used by humans is Decimal number system.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
52. 730.3899999999999864 Td
(For Ex: Let us consider decimal number 18. This number is represented in binary as 10010.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
52. 716.8899999999999864 Td
(We observe that binary number system take more digits to represent the decimal number. For large numbers we have to deal with very large binary strings. So this fact gave rise to three new number systems:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
52. 703.3899999999999864 Td
(i\) Octal number systems \(base 8\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
52. 689.8899999999999864 Td
(ii\) Hexa Decimal number system \(base 16\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
52. 676.3899999999999864 Td
(iii\) Binary Coded Decimal number \(BCD\) system) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
52. 654.8899999999999864 Td
(To define any number system we have to specify:) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
56. 641.3899999999999864 Td
(ï Base of the number system such as 2, 8, 10 or 16.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
56. 627.8899999999999864 Td
(ï The base decides the total number of digits available in that number system.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
56. 614.3899999999999864 Td
(ï First digit in the number system is always zero and last digit in the number system is always base-1.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.055 0.455 0.565 rg
